Single-database Alembic configuration for the Vote Without Doubt backend.

Authority
---------
This `migrations` directory is the **authoritative, versioned schema** for the
project. `backend/app/schema.sql` is a human-readable reference describing the
same tables; where the two disagree, the migrations are correct and
`schema.sql` is the defect.

Phase 1 remediation
-------------------
Phase 1 previously had no migration tooling at all: the app called
`db.create_all()` at startup inside a bare `except: pass`, so schema state could
neither be reviewed nor reproduced. Flask-Migrate + Alembic is now wired into the
app factory, `AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA` defaults to `False`, and the initial revision
(`initial schema from ORM metadata`) was generated from the ORM models.

Usage
-----
    cd backend

    # 1. point at your database
    #    MySQL (default):  set MYSQL_HOST / MYSQL_PORT / MYSQL_DATABASE /
    #                      MYSQL_USER / MYSQL_PASSWORD
    #    SQLite override: export DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./local.db
    export FLASK_ENV=development

    # 2. apply the schema
    venv/Scripts/python -m flask --app "app:create_app" db upgrade

    # 3. confirm the migration state matches the ORM models
    venv/Scripts/python -m flask --app "app:create_app" db check

Adding a migration
------------------
    venv/Scripts/python -m flask --app "app:create_app" db migrate -m "short description"

Always review the generated file in `versions/` before committing it, and run
`db upgrade` against a scratch database as well as the target one.